sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant User as Data Scientist / Client
    participant Router as OpenShift Router
    participant DSGW as data-science-gateway
    participant KAP as kube-auth-proxy
    participant Dash as odh-dashboard
    participant K8s as Kubernetes API
    participant WB as workbenches-operator + kubeflow
    participant KRP as kube-rbac-proxy
    participant KServe as kserve + odh-model-controller
    participant InfGW as openshift-ai-inference
    participant MaasGW as maas-default-gateway
    participant PExt as praxis-extproc
    participant Authz as Authorino / Limitador
    participant MaasAPI as maas-api
    participant EPP as llm-d EPP
    participant VLLM as vLLM pods

    Note over User,VLLM: Workflow A - Dashboard login and workbench access via data-science-gateway

    rect rgb(255, 240, 220)
    User->>Router: GET https://rh-ai.{domain}/ (HTTPS 443)
    Router->>DSGW: Reencrypt Route to gateway Service 443
    DSGW->>KAP: ext_authz HTTPS 8443 /oauth2/auth<br/>cookie + authorization headers
    alt No session
        KAP-->>User: 302 to OpenShift OAuth (user:full)
        User->>KAP: /oauth2/callback via oauth-callback-route
    else Session or valid Bearer
        KAP->>K8s: TokenReview (10s cache)
        KAP-->>DSGW: 2xx + x-auth-request-* + access token
    end
    Note over DSGW: Lua filter sets Authorization Bearer,<br/>strips _oauth2_proxy cookies.<br/>Fail closed, 5s timeout
    DSGW->>Dash: HTTPRoute rhods-dashboard<br/>HTTPS, DR insecureSkipVerify
    Dash->>K8s: Create Notebook CR with user token
    K8s->>WB: Mutating webhooks (Fail)<br/>hardwareprofile + connection injectors
    WB->>K8s: StatefulSet, Service, kube-rbac-proxy sidecar,<br/>HTTPRoute /notebook/ns/name + ReferenceGrant
    User->>DSGW: Open workbench (same ext_authz chain)
    DSGW->>KRP: HTTPS 8443 Bearer
    KRP->>K8s: TokenReview + SAR get notebooks/name
    KRP->>KRP: Proxy to Jupyter 8888
    end

    Note over User,VLLM: Workflow B - LLMInferenceService deployment and inference via openshift-ai-inference

    rect rgb(220, 235, 255)
    User->>Dash: Deploy LLM
    Dash->>KServe: List permitted gateways<br/>model-serving-api /api/v1/gateways (SSAR)
    Dash->>K8s: Create LLMInferenceService
    K8s->>KServe: Validating + mutating webhooks (Fail)
    KServe->>K8s: vLLM Deployment / LWS, InferencePool,<br/>llm-d EPP, HTTPRoute to openshift-ai-inference
    KServe->>K8s: Gateway AuthPolicy gateway-authn (TokenReview + SAR)<br/>EnvoyFilter gateway-authn-ssl (TLS to Authorino)
    User->>InfGW: POST /v1/chat/completions (HTTPS 443, Bearer)
    InfGW->>Authz: Kuadrant wasm, gRPC 50051 TLS
    Authz->>K8s: TokenReview + SAR get llminferenceservices
    Authz-->>InfGW: Allow
    InfGW->>EPP: ext_proc 9002 TLS
    Note over EPP: KV-cache, prefix and load scorers,<br/>optional P/D sidecar routing
    EPP-->>InfGW: Selected endpoint
    InfGW->>VLLM: Forward request
    Note over VLLM: Model servers have no built-in auth.<br/>NIXL KV transfer for P/D
    VLLM-->>User: Streaming completion
    end

    Note over User,VLLM: Workflow C - Governed inference via Models-as-a-Service

    rect rgb(225, 245, 225)
    User->>MaasGW: POST /v1/api-keys with OpenShift token<br/>maas-api-route
    MaasGW->>MaasAPI: HTTPS 8443, DR insecureSkipVerify
    MaasAPI-->>User: API key sk-oai-...
    User->>MaasGW: POST model path, Bearer sk-oai-... (HTTPS 443)
    MaasGW->>PExt: ext_proc ipp-pre 9004<br/>body model to header
    MaasGW->>Authz: AuthPolicy maas-gateway-auth
    Authz->>MaasAPI: /internal/v1/api-keys/validate<br/>NetworkPolicy-protected only
    Authz->>MaasAPI: /internal/v1/subscriptions/select
    Note over Authz: OPA subscription check, inject X-MaaS-* headers,<br/>deny client x-maas-*.<br/>Limitador TokenRateLimitPolicy + gateway-default-deny
    Authz-->>MaasGW: Allow + identity headers
    MaasGW->>PExt: ext_proc ipp 9004 (fail closed)<br/>provider resolution, usage enforcement
    alt Internal model
        MaasGW->>EPP: InferencePool endpoint pick
        EPP->>VLLM: Generate
        VLLM-->>MaasGW: Response stream
    else ExternalModel
        Note over MaasGW: ai-gateway-controller ServiceEntry +<br/>DR SIMPLE TLS + SNI, provider key injected
        MaasGW->>MaasGW: HTTPS 443 to external LLM provider
    end
    MaasGW->>PExt: Response through ext_proc (usage accounting)
    MaasGW-->>User: Completion
    end
